WEBVTT

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:06.090
FIT-IN
 BREAK

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.470
All right! Here we go!

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.370
What are you doing?

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:12.060
Is that a new sort of feint?

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.020
Shut up!

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.720
They look like they're having fun.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:22.700
Since Lunatic stopped their development, the streets are open as before.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.900
We have to be grateful to Mr. James, don't we?

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:34.750
Ah... Never mind.

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:36.500
Sela!

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.140
Okay! Nice pass!

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.690
It's like Sela's turned over a new leaf, right?

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.210
Maybe she finally cleared up the thing with her dad.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.100
To me it looks like she just enjoys being with Navi.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.580
If you can find someone you're attracted to, then you can fall in love with them.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:57.220
The worst are the jerks you have zero interest in.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.400
Are you talking about yourself and James?

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.660
I was young then too...

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.270
You want to hear?

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:09.770
Well, maybe I'll tell the story then.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.970
You know I lived in Mooneyes, right?

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.810
Long ago, on a kindergarten field trip,

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.890
we went to see the terminator line.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.300
Oh, isn't that...

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:27.940
That's the boundary between Mooneyes and the moon's far side, isn't it?

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:29.560
Exactly.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:34.310
On the moon though, it's a serious crime to cross the border and visit the far side.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.630
It gets you almost a life sentence behind bars.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.160
But that day, somehow I got lost.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:46.700
It was scary... I ran and ran, looking for everyone.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:51.700
Before I knew it, I'd trespassed into the moon's far side.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:00.460
Big footprints... A giant!

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:01.420
A giant?

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:05.650
Thinking back now, I was a babe in the woods.

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:09.410
Mooneyes has always kept the giants a secret.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:12.330
That's why they slapped us back down here.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:13.930
We did you a disservice.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.600
Well, never mind that.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:21.610
What I saw on the moon's far side was probably traces of a giant like Navi.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:25.540
If I'd been a grown-up, I'd have been arrested.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.570
But I was little, so they let me be.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:34.720
I mean, I could tell whoever I wanted that I'd seen a giant's footprints, and they'd never believe me.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:39.160
It made me so angry I could cry. Those footprints were all I could think about.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:43.090
And before I noticed, there I was, a shoe designer.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.970
It was around then that I first met James.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:52.810
He was the first person to ever listen to me talk about those footprints without laughing.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.540
And that's how he scored a first date.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:01.340
What? Did I say something funny?

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:05.250
Miss Haruka, you still like Mr. James, don't you?

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.570
Don't be an idiot! It's over between us!

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:10.510
Whatever you say.

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.210
Dan! Stop!

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.170
Miyuki?

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:16.830
What's wrong?

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:18.870
Soar, Dangan!

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:29.370
Gramps...

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.290
How's it looking, Miyuki?

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:33.260
Where's it broken?

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.820
It's the driver system in the foot.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.130
Can you fix it?

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:39.560
Yeah. The damage, anyway.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:40.490
But...

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.480
"But"?

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:44.480
Even if I fix it, some other part will just wear out next time.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.840
Just simple repair isn't gonna cut it.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:47.820
What do you mean?

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:53.490
Your skills as operators are starting to surpass these mechs' abilities.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:59.310
The Glamorous Bee, the Zephyr, and the Dangan...

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:04.000
They're all in the same condition to one degree or another.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.670
And take a look here.

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:09.270
That looks tasty!

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.470
No eating!

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:12.960
That's the reactor that powers a Bigfoot.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.780
Their power source is ultinium.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:19.850
And I don't know why, but their output has been increasing little by little lately.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:20.730
What's the deal?

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:22.060
Power-ups are good, right?

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:25.880
A runaway reactor is a lit stick of dynamite!

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.510
No, worse than that.

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:30.320
You can't leave something lying around with no idea when it's gonna blow up.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:34.070
Man, you really are smart.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.660
She's not like you, Dan.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:39.710
How are you going to deal with this?

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:44.080
A full overhaul and upgrade so they can keep up with how everyone plays.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:47.020
But there's a problem.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.040
A problem?

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.470
We can't do it with the facilities available here.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:54.430
It's not just that, Miyuki.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:02.480
To do the upgrade, we need specialized data from one other ultinium power system.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.440
<i>There</i>, you mean. {lit., you mean that place}

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:07.670
What do you mean, Miyuki? Where's there?

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:09.550
Area Zero.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.070
Sacred ground for Bigfoots...

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:16.340
It's the place where my father died.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.290
See for yourself, Your Majesty.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:24.170
Concert preparations are proceeding on schedule.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:30.660
If this Eclipse-or-whatever sings, then the stones will speak again?

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:35.820
Oh, I can guarantee that they will talk to you just as they used to do, Your Majesty.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:36.720
Truly?

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:40.430
I swear by the thunderbolt's power and the gods of Earth.

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:44.990
I see. I leave it to you, Yan Harris.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:03.440
The wind is weeping.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:07.210
A voice of never-healing sadness.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:12.100
Not bad, considering it was left to rot all those years.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.090
The system looks like it's still humming along.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:18.700
Access request: Takeshi Ayukawa.

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:21.390
File ID M1152.

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:26.830
"Ultinium Critical-Region Response Regulation and Inquiries...

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:30.130
...into Practical Application for Bigfoot Power Systems."

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:32.890
Executing request.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:35.560
This is...

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.880
The research data your father left behind.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:43.330
Yan.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:45.370
Hello there, you two.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:48.890
If you're here about the concert, could you take it to your new manager?

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:49.250
I'm—

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:52.260
Did we really make the right decision?

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:56.440
We decided to do the concert without mentioning it to Rouge...

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:59.580
We wonder if maybe she would be against it...

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:02.880
No need to worry, Violette.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:06.400
Rouge will abide by the decision you two have made.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:09.980
The future of the world depends on this concert, after all.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:14.770
We do it all for the sake of the new legend.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:18.990
On second look...

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:25.230
Wear like this couldn't be caused just by swinging the stick around.

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:26.480
Amazing.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:28.570
Oh, you see that, do you?

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:31.670
So what'll you do?

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:36.550
What? By herself?!

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:38.770
What do you mean, old man?

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:41.760
Buzz off. Ask Miyuki.

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.870
What's gotten into your head, Miyuki?

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:47.120
Do you even know how many days it'll take you to do it alone?

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:48.860
I want to basquat, not sit around!

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:49.840
And we gotta go to the moon—

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.220
Shut up!

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:53.940
You go take a nap and dream about that idol or something!

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.760
Wha—! Dumbass... Who'd...

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:59.820
Uh-oh Mr. Dan, your face is as red as can be.

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:03.470
Please!

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:05.430
This time, give me free rein!

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:09.830
Y-You don't have to ask!

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.990
Anyway, t-take care of it, okay? I'm leaving.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:14.110
Mr. Dan!

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:15.360
Don't call me Mr. Dan!

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:19.420
Miyuki, if you need any help let me know, okay?

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.440
I'm so hungry...

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.730
Suck it up, pretty boy.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.780
Something good'll happen sooner or later.

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:30.300
Ganz Bogard!

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:31.370
Bel Lindon!

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:32.660
What is it?

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:36.470
Who's that?

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:40.270
Is that... Princess Aurora?

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:42.250
The princess?!

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:51.510
Miss Miyuki, you haven't eaten yet?

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:55.710
Leave it over there. I'll eat it later.

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:57.650
Miss Miyuki...

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:03.020
Is Miyuki coming?

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:09.260
I know she's determined, but she's pushing herself too hard.

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:12.270
Suddenly saying that she wants to do the work by herself...

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:15.870
She doesn't eat, and it doesn't look like she sleeps much.

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:17.950
She'll wreck her health if she goes on like this.

00:09:19.670 --> 00:09:23.040
Let that child do as she wishes, please.

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:28.990
Right now Miyuki is trying to raise her level as an engineer.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:33.470
You've all advanced, and in order to meet and respond to the way you all play,

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:36.070
she has to improve her skills as well.

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:38.420
That's what that child decided.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:42.050
Dan!

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:44.800
Work too hard, and you'll collapse of exhaustion.

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:50.850
A-Alan and the rest are worried about you.

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:53.270
You took a bite of this.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:55.440
You've been skipping meals, right?

00:09:55.440 --> 00:10:00.320
Yeah. But I want to get these babies fixed as quick as I can.

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:04.370
I want to take the data my Dad left behind and have it serve everyone.

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:10.460
A long time ago, I worked at Lunatic doing research on ultinium.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:15.380
The reactor that powers Bigfoots now is a system I developed then.

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:20.590
My son Takeshi was trying to develop that system even further.

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:23.510
Develop it by making it even more high-powered, or what?

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:29.550
No, Takeshi was trying to use machines to recreate the giants of legend.

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:35.530
But sometimes technology surpasses human knowlege and runs wild,

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:37.690
and leaves deep scars.

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:41.440
Dad!

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:45.290
I understood, intellectually.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:50.740
New technologies bring with them new accidents. I understood that.

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:57.720
If we deserve to go through that kind of pain to learn the truth of the world,

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:01.380
people must be fools.

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:15.980
I wonder why Miss Miyuki wanted to follow in her father's footsteps after he passed away.

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:19.810
I sort of get why she would do that.

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:24.830
She must have wanted to feel something of her father through her work.

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:27.580
Feel her father...

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:36.130
Gramps created Bigfoots as labor-saving devices to improve quality of life.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:41.000
He's always taught me that the work of an engineer...

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:45.210
...is to look at what I can do to make Bigfoots bring people happiness.

00:11:45.210 --> 00:11:50.790
So Dan, when we learned that Coco lost her ability to walk because of a Bigfoot,

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:54.690
me and Gramps both doubted ourselves.

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:58.020
If there were no Bigfoots, it would never have happened, right?

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:02.130
"Technology is just like sake!"

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:06.680
"If you drink and drink without knowing your own limit, someday it'll destroy you!"

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:09.820
What's that? An impression of your grandpa?

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:16.010
Basically it means that the pursuit of technology itself becomes your goal.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.920
I don't understand this confusing stuff.

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:23.880
But I don't hate Bigfoots any more.

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:29.370
If there were no Bigfoots, we wouldn't be here now,

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:31.820
and we'd never have started playing Basquash.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:33.850
Everybody smiled, right?

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:36.470
They only could because of Bigfoots.

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:41.230
I'm grateful to your grandpa, though I'll die before I say so.

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:43.610
Dan...

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:45.550
Eat your grub.

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:47.000
Let's go, Spanky.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:48.540
Huh? Grub?

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.590
I wanna eat something good...

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:52.330
Bel's share is left over.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:03.480
He's asleep.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:04.730
That's okay.

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:25.150
O wind, O clouds, O earth...

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:29.610
Carry a song of peace to the souls that were lost.

00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:34.610
Sela!

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:36.860
Practicing by yourself?

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:38.710
It doesn't count as practice...

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:39.990
I just have nothing to do.

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:41.690
Then...

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.120
I don't mind keeping you company.

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.560
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:49.830
I'm twiddling my thumbs too, that's all. {alt tl: I don't have anything to do either.}

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:50.670
But...

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:55.390
It certainly doesn't mean that I want to play Basquash with you or anything.

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:59.530
What's so funny?!

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:02.620
How are you going to practice without a Bigfoot?

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:06.420
You're a big silly.

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:09.150
If you want to be with him, you could just say so.

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:10.480
Crawly!

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:17.580
It's not <i>that</i> funny!

00:14:18.510 --> 00:14:19.870
Sorry...

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:22.030
Catch me caring!

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:26.870
I'm sorry, Sela! I won't laugh any more, just don't be mad!

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:32.520
Good, good!

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:34.480
Miyuki won't beat me!

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:39.470
This is a chance to perfect my Super-Sole Pattern and all-weather tracing system!

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:41.900
There's so much to do!

00:14:55.070 --> 00:14:57.250
Princess, is something the matter?

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:59.200
You look a bit downhearted.

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:03.180
Jiiya, do you think I can go on like this?

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:04.950
What do you mean?

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:10.160
When they ask themselves what they ought to do, they all have a clear answer.

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:15.380
But me... What do I think I'm doing?

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:17.330
Princess...

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:21.200
I can't just stay as I am, can I?

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:30.230
Taking a break?

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:31.860
{oh sound}Gramps!

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.430
You're just in time.

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:34.400
Look at this.

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:37.160
Right here, in Dad's charts.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:39.270
A bunch of parts they ought to show are missing.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:43.070
You're right. I never noticed.

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:46.940
And the energy regulator is directly coupled to the core.

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:49.460
{laughs}What a sneaky bastard!

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.150
You knew?

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.930
It's something my son would do.

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.810
What? What?

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:59.090
Weren't you gonna do this on your own?

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:05.890
Well, I guess I can favor my adorable granddaughter with a hint.

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:09.320
The purpose of a chart is to impart a concept to other people,

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:12.180
but it's also to keep your own self from forgetting.

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:19.360
Takeshi didn't draw those parts on the chart because he had no fear of forgetting them.

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:20.610
I get it!

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:23.320
The first coefficient — it's a physical constant, isn't it?

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:25.720
The speed of light? Pi?

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:28.090
No, Dad was an engineer, so...

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:30.500
The energy conversion efficiency? The coefficient of friction?!

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:36.470
Let's see... three blocks are missing, so it must be a three-vector matrix!

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:38.890
What doesn't change, what doesn't change...

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:42.080
A constant tensile strength... a constant base value!

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:47.640
<i>Minamoto Yoshitsune: a famous samurai in Japanese history who led a victorious attack against the Taira clan in Valley One (Ichi no Tani)</i>

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:47.640
Ichi no Tani!

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:47.640
Yoshitsune! {sz: I have no idea what they're going on about, except maybe they're pretending to be invading generals or something.}

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:51.230
My surprise attack...

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:52.940
...has failed.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:05.130
Princess...

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:10.600
Look! These are my masterpieces!

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:15.300
But they look exactly the same.

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.890
The insides! Insides!

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:21.170
From the windshield to the fingertips, the insides are completely different!

00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:24.020
If you're going to complain, do it <i>after</i> you've tried them out!

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:30.020
She says the insides are different, but this is totally the same...

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:32.180
How's it different?

00:17:38.420 --> 00:17:39.280
This...

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:42.150
Amazing!

00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:44.860
Well? Noticed the difference?

00:17:44.860 --> 00:17:47.120
Yes. There's no unnecessary motion.

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:51.140
And the motions they do make are smooth as silk, with no jerkiness at all.

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:54.610
To the discerning eye, the difference is night and day.

00:17:56.390 --> 00:17:57.370
Light...

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:02.040
That's good work.

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.060
You've grown up.

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:06.180
I bet Takeshi is happy right about now.

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:10.310
Gramps...

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:20.360
Awesome! I've never seen Bigfoots like these before!

00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:22.870
The kinesthetics are completely different!

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:25.790
It's like my nerves run all the way to her fingertips!

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:27.320
It's incredible, Miss Miyuki!

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:30.700
You really are something to reckon with, Miyuki!

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:31.120
So—

00:18:33.330 --> 00:18:34.760
She's tired.

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:35.870
Let's let her sleep.

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:39.250
Working too hard.

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:46.740
All right! These'll take us straight to Mooneyes!

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:48.350
Just you wait!

00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:54.630
What is this?

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:58.690
These are memories. Things I remember.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.580
Who am I?

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:02.690
I'm Rouge.

00:19:03.710 --> 00:19:05.570
I know those people.

00:19:05.980 --> 00:19:08.060
Citron. Violette.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:11.450
Friends I value very much.

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:13.830
Rouge!

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:16.210
Dan!

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:18.710
No!

00:19:18.710 --> 00:19:19.740
No!

00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:21.210
Stop!

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:24.650
No!

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:32.680
Good morning, Rouge.

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:37.640
I'm... Rouge.

00:19:38.270 --> 00:19:40.230
How does it feel to be reborn?

00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:41.820
Feel?

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:44.260
I don't know.

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:48.930
Hey... Why am I crying?

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:51.540
Don't worry about it.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:53.880
You must have dreamed of something sad.

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.260
That happens all the time.

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:58.190
Contact General Manager Yan Harris.

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:01.750
Let him know that Rouge's preparations are complete.

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:02.330
Yes, ma'am.

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:05.640
A sad dream...?

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:12.510
Dad, Gramps said I did good.

00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:14.960
He said I'm grown up.

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:17.300
You can see them, right?

00:20:17.680 --> 00:20:19.980
All your children.

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:23.960
One day they'll go to the moon too.

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:29.150
Dan, come quick!

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:30.620
Sela?

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:36.660
The upcoming concert in the Skybloom Kingdom will be Eclipse's last before we disband.

00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:38.900
Not Eclipse...

00:20:39.350 --> 00:20:41.710
My Eclipse...

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:42.540
Passport... {sz: getting weepy about "Moon Passport" I think}

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:46.210
Everyone, watch us until the end!

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:48.060
Disband...

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:50.410
Rouge!

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:54.210
Everyones own path,

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:55.950
Everyones own decision,

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:57.210
I....

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:58.290
I...

00:20:58.990 --> 00:21:00.560
must decide what to do

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:02.320
must watch what I do

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:06.190
Next time: TOTAL ECLIPSE.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:06.190
NEXT TIME

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:05.060
TOTAL ECLIPSE

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:06.780
TOTAL ECLIPSE
